    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can postmenopause cause weight gain?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Postmenopause can contribute to weight gain, especially around the abdomen. Lower estrogen, reduced muscle mass, insulin resistance, poor sleep, inflammation, thyroid issues, and lower recovery capacity can all affect how your body stores fat and responds to diet and exercise."
      }
    },
    {
